From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:41:40 -0400
Subject: sidebar: hide it completely, pins join the end, the edge resizes

The operator's pass on beta 12 asked for a third sidebar form and named
three faults; each is built here and was seen working on the real
window, and what that use found is fixed too.

- A third form (sidebar Y19). "When the sidebar closes: Shrink to
  icons / Hide it completely" (stedding.sidebar.closed_form) decides
  what Ctrl+S, the toggle and dragging the edge closed leave. Hidden,
  the strip takes no width (CollapsedWidthNow) and the page card keeps
  no gutter and no rounded corner (SteddingCardGutter, read by the
  card, the address row, the window's bar and the frame's caption
  buttons): the page and the row run edge to edge. The pointer resting
  at the window's leading edge slides the sidebar in over the page by
  expand-on-hover's float; leaving it slides it away. While closed or
  sliding, the strip clips its rows, which painted over the page from
  layers of their own. The command bar has Show Sidebar, Collapse
  Sidebar to Icons and Hide Sidebar.
- Space pins (pins H14). A new pin joins the end of the pinned run; an
  unpin goes to the top of the tabs under the Clear line. A pin went to
  the top of the run, and an unpin from its middle split it, so the
  pins below it were laid out under the line as ordinary tabs.
- The resize edge (sidebar Y18). The handle reaches over the card's
  gutter to the card's edge through the strip's event targeters; it
  stopped a gutter short of the edge a person aims at.
- Settings (T13, T14). The Stedding page reads in sections, Sidebar
  first, with the new choice, the width, the tab row height (the
  density, renamed) and the text size together.
- Found by using it: the rail's toggle sat over an empty band, because
  the hidden combo's buttons were still counted (Y20); a strip drawn
  open while closed by state keeps the open top row; the selected
  row's default globe was the light scheme's on the dark sidebar, a
  translucent row read by its own channels (S-73, Y21); the toggle's
  tooltip and the command bar named Chromium 155's Ctrl+Shift+L, now
  unbound (S-87); a page's own full screen and F11 with no address row
  kept the card's gutter (S-69, toolbar T33).
- Found by reading the diff before the cut: the edge reveals only a
  sidebar the window shows and only if the pointer is still there; right
  to left, the edge and the handle's reach are the right-hand ones; in
  macOS full screen a visible sidebar keeps its gutter and a hidden one
  insets nothing; a strip of no width never puts the page past the
  window's edge; a selection's tabs already pinned or unpinned stay put.
- From the backlog: the screenshot toast says "Show in folder" off the
  Mac (S-83); the shortcut list drops Peek's rows while Peek is off and
  says the ninth row chord goes to the last row (S-82).

Why: the operator's requests on beta 12, and the faults found while
building them; each has its behaviour id and a test.
Removable when: never; this is Stedding's sidebar.
